      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MUMMSIE (4) is the one to beat after putting together two decisive wins here, most recently scoring by just over five lengths in BM54 grade as a well-supported favourite. The 1600m record is the only question, with four placings and no wins at around the trip, but her current form and light weight keep her clearly on top. MATRON SAMSING (3) has the right form to challenge, having won at Kununurra before missing by a nose in Open company at this track, and her 1600m record is stronger than most of these. GRINZINGER LASS (5) was only beaten two and a half lengths in that same Open, with a steadied run adding context, though the extra ground still asks something of her. PRINCESS PANCAKES (2) beat MATRON SAMSING last start and has solid 1600m form, but turning that narrow Open win into another from the outside draw is the task.",
